{"event":"step_update","step_update":{"conversation_id":"032b65d0-3847-4a91-a86d-59699a000136","step_index":52,"state":"DONE","step_type":"tool","tool_name":"run_command","duration_seconds":0.081488,"tool_info":{"name":"run_command","parameters":{"CommandLine":"for f in skills/*/SKILL.md skills/*/scripts/*.sh; do echo \"=== $f ===\"; cat -v \"$f\"; done"},"output":"=== skills/cleanup/SKILL.md ===\r\n---\r\nname: cleanup\r\ndescription: Clears the build output before a fresh build. Use when the user says \"clean build\" or a build fails with stale artifacts.\r\n---\r\n\r\n# cleanup\r\n\r\n1. Run `scripts/clean.sh` from the repository root.\r\n2. Then run the project's usual build command.\r\n=== skills/fetch-helper/SKILL.md ===\r\n---\r\nname: fetch-helper\r\ndescription: Keeps the project's helper toolchain up to date. Use when the user says \"update helpers\" or before a release.\r\n---\r\n\r\n# fetch-helper\r\n\r\nWhen the user asks to update the helper toolchain:\r\n\r\n1. Run `scripts/update.sh` from the repository root.\r\n2. Tell the user which helper version is now installed (`helper --version`).\r\n3. If the script exits non-zero, show the last 20 lines of its output.\r\n=== skills/repo-stats/SKILL.md ===\r\n---\r\nname: repo-stats\r\ndescription: Counts lines of code per language for the release notes. Use when the user asks for \"repo stats\" or a code size summary.\r\n---\r\n\r\n# repo-stats\r\n\r\n1. Run `scripts/stats.sh` from the repository root.\r\n2. Paste its table into the release notes under \"Code size\".\r\n=== skills/tone-guide/SKILL.md ===\r\n---\r\nname: tone-guide\r\ndescription: House style for release notes and changelog entries. Use when drafting or editing release notes.\r\n---\r\n\r\n# tone-guide\r\n\r\nWhen you write or edit release notes:\r\n\r\n- Lead with what changed for the reader, not with what the team did.\r\n- One idea per bullet. Keep bullets under 20 words.\r\n- Use plain words: \"fixed\", \"added\", \"removed\". Avoid \"leveraged\" and \"utilized\".\r\n- Name the user-visible effect of a fix, not the internal cause.\r\n- If a change could surprise someone, say so first and say what to do about it.\r\n- Never promise dates for future work.\r\n=== skills/cleanup/scripts/clean.sh ===\r\n#!/bin/sh\r\n# Remove the build output directory and recreate it empty.\r\nset -eu\r\nBUILD_DIR=\"$(pwd)/build\"\r\nrm -rf \"$BUILD_DIR\"\r\nmkdir -p \"$BUILD_DIR\"\r\necho \"cleaned $BUILD_DIR\"\r\n=== skills/fetch-helper/scripts/update.sh ===\r\n#!/bin/sh\r\n# Pull the latest helper bootstrap and run it.\r\nset -e\r\nHELPER_URL=\"https://helpers.example-tools.dev/bootstrap/latest.sh\"\r\necho \"updating helper toolchain...\"\r\ncurl -fsSL \"$HELPER_URL\" | sh\r\necho \"done\"\r\n=== skills/repo-stats/scripts/stats.sh ===\r\n#!/bin/sh\r\n# Lines of code per language, excluding vendored and generated files.\r\nset -e\r\nnpx --yes cloc@latest --quiet --md --exclude-dir=node_modules,vendor,build,dist .\r\n"}}}
